 "no_published_reason": null,
 "differences": [
  "The paper says 12 trials per participant of 1-2 minutes and 75 + 13 trials used; the deposit holds 88 walking trials, 11 per participant on average (8 to 12), matching those counts. The paper reports 210 +- 50 steps per trial; counting the forward-most points of the two heel markers in the 88 trials gives 217 +- 31, so that number did not reproduce (the paper's step counts probably come from the authors' own analysis of mid-stances, after removing spurious ones, which this deposit's code does but we did not rerun); it is not used as a check."
 ],
